    "narrative": "The offensive outlook for Ghost Ride the WHIP on September 11 reflects a premium on middle-of-the-order run production and situational advantages against volatile starters. **Josh Naylor** (72.05) leads the charge as our strongest play, benefiting from a soft matchup against Jeffrey Springs. **Naylor** thrives in this environment, with a +19% boost derived from the opposing starter's profile and a favorable park factor, positioning him as the centerpiece of today\u2019s scoring efforts. He is closely trailed by **Trevor Story** (68.66) and **Brice Turang** (68.60); **Turang** earns his high floor through a #2 lineup slot and a +19% SP skill boost, while **Story** leverages a +7% park factor and aggressive baserunning potential to remain a must-start despite the presence of Lugo. **James Wood** (66.53) also commands attention; despite a slightly tougher test against Yusei Kikuchi, his elite xwOBA (.415) and prime #1 lineup position offer the highest ceiling for volume and run production today.\n\nThe most difficult decision on the bench involved **Austin Riley** (56.13), who finished just shy of the active roster threshold. While **Riley** boasts an elite BvP history (65 PA), the optimizer favored the higher park-adjusted floors provided by **Max Muncy** and the current platoon-aligned efficiency of **Vinnie Pasquantino**. **Pasquantino** (67.51) remains in the UTIL slot specifically because of a +14% dynamic platoon edge against Gray. We are closely monitoring the lineup statuses for **Gabriel Moreno**, **Josh Naylor**, **Brice Turang**, **Cole Young**, **Max Muncy**, **Jose Caballero**, **Corbin Carroll**, and **Griffin Conine**, as these pending confirmations introduce non-zero risk to the projected order-based bonuses. Furthermore, while **Corbin Carroll** (64.61) carries a solid score, his outlook is buoyed by a +4% boost due to a slow-delivery opposing pitcher, which we hope facilitates a productive day on the basepaths. Conversely, **Jose Caballero** remains a marginal start (45.87) due to a significant platoon disadvantage and a bottom-tier lineup position that tempers his overall efficiency.",
